## 4.2.1 (2026-09-05)

A small release. One of these is a bug you could actually walk into; the
rest is the history page getting faster and some dead code from the HeroUI
v3 migration coming out.

### Bugs fixed:

-   the help links in the Ollama and OpenAI settings navigated the settings window itself to ollama.com, out of the app, with no way back. They open in your browser now, like every other link in Gloss. The prop that used to make them external stopped meaning anything in the interface rewrite and nothing had noticed
-   searching the history rescanned the whole table twice on every keystroke, rebuilding the two filter dropdowns from an answer that cannot change while you type. On a 20k-row history that was 9ms of the ~13ms each keystroke spent in the database; it is 3ms now, once, when the page opens. Filtering by service or target no longer sorts the whole matching set to show you twenty rows

### Removed:

-   the OpenAI settings carried an ad for a third-party API reseller, in Chinese regardless of your language, behind a referral link crediting pot's author. A settings page is a poor place to advertise and it was not ours to profit from

### Internal:

-   TypeScript 7, so `pnpm typecheck` runs on the native compiler
-   the props HeroUI v3 quietly ignores are gone from the four components still passing them; one of them was reaching the DOM and warning about it on every test run
